            <ArticleTitle>Changing controversies in surgery for angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-8, 20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery surgery has evolved rapidly since its introduction 20 years ago. Few operations have been subjected to such scrutiny. As a result many details of prognosis have been clarified, but the development of coronary angioplasty, thrombolysis and the internal mammary artery graft have created new controversies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
